A||||3||Frank Sombers||Sound proofing/heat shield?||||1||
Z||000000||Frank Sombers||12-05-2000||07:29 PM||||I have an '88 cpe. with a 5 speed. What is the function of the fibreglass material glued on the sides of the engine bay? Is it for heat protection or simply used to deaden road noise? The material on my right side is falling apart and off, and I want to replace it. If it provides heat protection I was thinking of replacing it with aluminized heat barrier material. Thanks for your time and opinions.<BR>Frank||||reg||1
Z||000001||Mark||12-05-2000||09:10 PM||||Frank,<P>It's main function is to hold dirt, get frayed, and look bad.  But actually, I believe it's there for noise reduction.  I removed mine from the right (battery) side and noticed no increase in engine noise.   ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Rodrv6||12-05-2000||09:59 PM||||I took both sides out of my 84 years ago and couldn't tell any difference in noise.  It makes the engine bay MUCH easier to keep clean and nice looking.<P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  84 SE, 330,000 miles and counting :)||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||12-06-2000||09:38 PM||||Removing it from the sides won't hurt anything. If you remove the stuff from the front tho the interior may get hotter and/or be loader.||||reg||1
